<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX NOAILLES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX NOAILLES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group two Prix</p>
<p>Noailles for three-year-old colts and fillies run over one mile</p>
<p>and three furlongs (2.2 kms) at Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Fragrant Mix (ridden by Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>2. Sendoro (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p>3. Shaka (Jean-Rene Dubosc)</p>
<p>4. Keroub (Sylvain Guillot)</p>
<p>6 ran</p>
<p>Distances: 3 lengths, half</p>
<p>Winner owned by Jean-Luc Lagardere and trained in France by</p>
<p>Andre Fabre.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 55,336 dollars</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (includes a one-franc stake): Win 3.50; places</p>
<p>1.90, 1.80. Straight Forecast 12.70</p>
</text>
